{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals","id":901159,"title":"Too many supernaturals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T10:53:47-07:00","id":901159,"title":"Too many supernaturals?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> (This might be rambling a bit, bear with me please)<br /> <br /> <br /> The default Chronicles of Darkness idea is that is &quot;our world but (supernaturally) grim&quot;, and this supernatural is caused by several beings from mythology and such; my peeve is that currently there are too many supernatural beings and societies to be secret! We have: Vampires, Mages, Werewolves, Changelings, Sin-Eaters, Mummies, Beasts, low-power psychic/magicians/skinchangers, ghosts, spirits, etc.<br /> <br /> The secret keeping powers and effects (The lie, mascarade, Lunacy, Mask, etc) can account for people not knowing in an individual basis, the problem is aggregation, CoD is supersaturated with suernatural beings, which since have become so abundant and numerous, are no longer SUPERnatural (definition: <i>departing from what is usual or normal</i> especially so as to appear to transcend the laws of nature)<br /> <br /> In a chronicle that assumes all the gamelines are valid, isn't the world overpopulated with magical beings?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:00:28-07:00","id":901164,"title":"","content":"There're a lot of different kinds of supernaturals but they're either really difficult to see or perceive (spirits, ghosts, angels etc) or comparatively rare (the major splats). In a city of, say 100,000 people, maybe 750 of those or fewer are supernaturals, most of them relatively minor players (and most of them won't be around for long, given the way that the supernatural world tends to chew through newbies). Those numbers are just guesses, but some splats are more common than other. Vampires are more common than mages and sin-eaters, who are more common than Prometheans and changelings who are more common than Beasts and there are maybe a thousand or so Arisen worldwide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:13:49-07:00","id":901180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901164#post901164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There're a lot of different kinds of supernaturals but they're either really difficult to see or perceive (spirits, ghosts, angels etc) or comparatively rare (the major splats). In a city of, say 100,000 people, maybe 750 of those or fewer are supernaturals, most of them relatively minor players (and most of them won't be around for long, given the way that the supernatural world tends to chew through newbies). Those numbers are just guesses, but some splats are more common than other. Vampires are more common than mages and sin-eaters, who are more common than Prometheans and changelings who are more common than Beasts and there are maybe a thousand or so Arisen worldwide.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct, but to analyse it a little furthermore? Humans confronted by supernatural happenstance are often subjected to breaking points (read: throwing dice to see in which scale of insanity, real or perceived, they fall). The very few that decide to actively confront this new reality usually take up the Vigil. It's not an easy path, it's not a common path, and despite specific efforts made to expose these truths, another truth is that the general public doesn't wants to believe that horrific things go bump in the night.<br /> <br /> There's a saying that goes &quot;The worst blind person is the one which doesn't wants to see the obvious&quot;. That's the general populace.<br /> <br /> That's without discussing the considerable avenues that the different supernatural conspiracies have to conceal their affairs. Concealment infrastructures, spiritual rites, the default enmity of the collective unconscious with the idea that they aren't but lambs amid the wolves which makes someone professing this to be considered utterly insane... Ect, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> If you think that's too much to bear, spend an hour reading over some conspiracy theories OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:43:34-07:00","id":901211,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is that there is not one CofD setting. Which is to say, the cosmology for each gameline does not line up with the others neatly, which brings us to the following bit that separates CofD from the WoD:<br /> -A supernatural creature only exists if you want it to.<br /> <br /> The main consequence of that? If you're playing Vampire: the Requiem then the only supernaturals that definitely exist are Vampires and Ghouls. All the gamelines are compatible rules-wise but there's no inbuilt assumption that every type of supernatural exists in any specific world.<br /> <br /> I know many people like to take CofD as a kitchen sink world and assume that everything lives in the same universe, and that's a fine view, but at least the 1e gamelines were more toolkits than settings, and even in 2e there's no 'this game takes place in a setting which also includes werewolves and mages and demons and beasts' even with the tighter settings*. I know I don't like to run a game with just Vampires (I'll through in some small 'm' non-awakened mortal mages as well, and probably some type of spirits or demons), but there's no reason to assume that X exists just because they appear in another gameline.<br /> <br /> * Not more specific as such, but tighter thematically, I found Requiem 1e to be rather bland but Requiem 2e really highlighted the struggle for me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:44:20-07:00","id":901213,"title":"","content":"Looking at how much strange stuff we hear about in reality, you could actually argue there are too few supernatural beings in WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:08:09-07:00","id":901241,"title":"","content":"Even by that definition of supernatural, the supernatural are still supernatural. The ones that outnumber mortals are spirits and ghosts and other beings, which 'appear to transcend the laws of nature.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals#post901159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a chronicle that assumes all the gamelines are valid, isn't the world overpopulated with magical beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a problem with that you can choose not to run a chronicle that assumes all the gamelines are valid.<br /> <br /> Or you can harass people who do and insist that you believe they're wrong whenever they post about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:14:02-07:00","id":901251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901241#post901241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can harass people who do and insist that you believe they're wrong whenever they post about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't thinks this was really warranted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T13:47:55-07:00","id":901340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901164#post901164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There're a lot of different kinds of supernaturals but they're either really difficult to see or perceive (spirits, ghosts, angels etc) or comparatively rare (the major splats). In a city of, say 100,000 people, maybe 750 of those or fewer are supernaturals, most of them relatively minor players (and most of them won't be around for long, given the way that the supernatural world tends to chew through newbies). Those numbers are just guesses, but some splats are more common than other. Vampires are more common than mages and sin-eaters, who are more common than Prometheans and changelings who are more common than Beasts and there are maybe a thousand or so Arisen worldwide.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually I think Changelings are more common then Sib Eaters, perhaps closer in sizexto mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T13:50:11-07:00","id":901343,"title":"","content":"Also I think world governments also help cover stuff up, not just the supernatural communities themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T13:57:34-07:00","id":901353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901340#post901340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I think Changelings are more common then Sib Eaters, perhaps closer in sizexto mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, I'm not an expert in supernatural demographics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:05:11-07:00","id":901364,"title":"","content":"The impression I get from the books is that most people do know about the supernatural, they just do their best not to learn too much about it. There are people who won't go into a dark room for fear of what might be waiting for them, but they have no specific idea of what that might be and turn a blind eye to finding out (unless its the hard way). Organized government agencies would probably know but then they are part of the system that keeps people ignorant.<br /> \u200bRemember, it's easy to hide a thousand among a forest of millions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:09:03-07:00","id":901369,"title":"","content":"I believe that in terms of major templates, werewolves were the most populous owing due to their well, ability to actually reproduce via conventional means, but it's balanced out by a high casualty rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:13:34-07:00","id":901382,"title":"","content":"Given that a lot of supernatural encounters crack one's Integrity, often sparking a personal crisis, most people avoid the memory or its implications. For some this sparks a downward spiral that ends in death, addiction, or insanity. Others end up Cassandras, dismissed as to escape the truth. More than should join up, with mystery cults or hunters, and try to insulate others from monstrosities in the shadows. A few take the capitalist route, and write books and films and tv shows, which get popularized and dismissed and dissected add mythmaking, which ends up de-legitimizing anyone who declaims the honest truth as lost romantics or paranoids, and their low Integrities bear that out.<br /> <br /> So, maybe all the monsters are there, and we're too broken to care. Look at the opioid overdoses, the demonization of innocents, millions on head meds, and wonder if we've seen enough to be afraid, but chose to be afraid if the wrong things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:51:12-07:00","id":901423,"title":"","content":"Supernatural societies are neither universally present nor evenly distributed; 1e's signature cities stuck to one splat per locale for more reasons than just wordcount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901369#post901369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that in terms of major templates, werewolves were the most populous owing due to their well, ability to actually reproduce via conventional means, but it's balanced out by a high casualty rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in 1e it was an unreliably-expressed latent trait that didn't even get consistently passed along at the carrier level. Werewolf genetics intersects with spiritual metaphysics in a way that doesn't require a particularly high turnover rate to justify global numbers below seven digits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:48:03-07:00","id":901476,"title":"","content":"Most supernatural beings, the major templates at least, remain hidden from the world to such a degree that they often are hidden from each other. It is not a certainty that all templates are aware of each other by default. There may be many beings in a city but they are all hiden from each other.<br /> <br /> The majob exception to this point are beasts. All others must learn of other denizens of darkness and how to find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T02:12:33-07:00","id":901892,"title":"","content":"... And we have in <b>Mage</b> there is Lie and Curse of Sleep - Quiescence. In game, humanity is cursed to suffer after seeing supernatural - Supernal in particular - so they would not see past Lie of universe. In my books, it's official answer on &quot;seeing monster leads to Breaking Point&quot; and why society of humans do not acknowledged existence of supernatural - &quot;&lt; Auto memory editing on seeing spells and displacement of seeing monster &gt; It's crazies talk, you silly goose...&quot;<br /> <br /> I advise to read <b>Mage</b> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ill-lie-to-you/\" target=\"_blank\">blog post about Lie</a> - it helps to understand CoD universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T05:02:31-07:00","id":901958,"title":"","content":"I see a situation like this -<br /> <br /> Three friends spend the weekend trapped in a Haunted House of Terror, and are subjected to all sorts of supernatural phenomena over the course of 2 days and barely escape with their lives.<br /> <br /> Character A remembers everything, and goes rushing to Cops and the Media. Her story is outlandish by conventional wisdom, and will likely be dismissed by most credible authorities. Even the other people that were there can't (or won't) back up her story. There is even a good chance that a supernatural conspirator in the Police or Media will actively smear her credibility to prevent her stories from ever being taken seriously. She knows what she saw and can't let it go. If she keeps pursuing the mysteries of what she experienced, she will wind up dead, broken, or become part of the darkness herself. Her response is the rarest - while she makes a good protagonist in a game or story, she is an unusual outlier in most mortal populations.<br /> <br /> Character B also remembers everything, but if asked will lie about it and blame perfectly mundane reasons for his injuries. He believes that there is nothing to be gained and so much to lose by meddling with the supernatural, especially since he was lucky to survive his last encounter. He will likely spend the rest of his days noticing the hand prints of the supernatural in ways he never noticed before, but will do nothing. He might carry that burden of knowledge but continue to live pretty normal live. Or the secrets and paranoia will slowly eat away at him. His response is considered a common reaction. Even if you do not account for the major templates and documented creatures, the CofD is still crawling with strangeness that doesn't fit into a neat box. If you are a regular, vulnerable mortal, the only safe, sane, and probably wise response is to ignore it, go on with your life, and Never.Speak.Of.It.Again.<br /> <br /> Character C will remember very little, and rationalize the rest. There are powerful forces at work in the world that conceal the supernatural from mortal eyes. Even if their weren't , a typical humans mind trembles when confronted by supernatural events. Their memories will be hazy or entirely missing, they will alter details and rationalize events. Anything to make their experience easier to deal with on a mental and emotional level. This effect is so basic and widespread that even individuals with the personality and capability to expose the supernatural world might not remember their experience enough to act on it. And this is like the response for the bulk of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T05:58:54-07:00","id":901973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901476#post901476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most supernatural beings, the major templates at least, remain hidden from the world to such a degree that they often are hidden from each other. It is not a certainty that all templates are aware of each other by default. There may be many beings in a city but they are all hiden from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is no longer true in 2e. Vampires can instantly tell someone is a werewolf, mage, changeling, and I believe Beast on sight*. Werewolf wolf senses can detect other supernaturals and sniff them out. Mages have their Sights. Changelings and their Kenning seem to pick up on magical beings much like Mage Sight does. Beasts can auto-detect supernaturals as part of their template. <br /> <br /> This pretty much leaves things in Twilight or Demons as the only possible &quot;hidden from each other&quot; supernatural types by default. If you want to hide from the at-large supernatural community, you need to invest in Obfuscate, strengthen your Mask, and use other hiding powers. The default is knowing each other rather than not.<br /> <br /> That's why STs need to decide what supernaturals exist in a given game rather than assume they're all in. Or the distribution. Even if you include mages in your vampire game, if their isn't a major Mystery in the city, chances are there's no local mage society. Werewolves tend to be spread out and claim large tracks of land as territory, keeping all other wolves (and Hosts) out. There's only a handful of Mummies in the entire world, and they spend most of their time asleep - honestly, I'm still hardpressed to figure out how they can have a society or guilds or anything.<br /> <br /> My big issue with the CofD crossover, however? Exarchs versus God Machine versus Judges, etc. Just how many different god-level supernaturals claim to control the world and its fate? Why aren't they at war with each other, considering they're not working together? There are just too many world spanning powers that control everything to the point it doesn't all fit. I don't think we can have them all working in the same setting, even with the whole &quot;shrouded in mystery&quot; bits. Something has to give.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Vampires' Predator Aura ability detect anyone with auras automatically, so that means they can instantly tell werewolves and mages. The Changeling playtest material shows that anyone with supernatural senses instantly sees past the Mask. And I believe that any supernatural can see the Horror super-imposed over the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:25:33-07:00","id":901989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901241#post901241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a problem with that you can choose not to run a chronicle that assumes all the gamelines are valid.<br /> <br /> Or you can harass people who do and insist that you believe they're wrong whenever they post about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I am harassing people? I made a question, explained why I think so, and waited for answers... At which point did I claim &quot;I am right, all must agree with my point&quot; ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901973#post901973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's only a handful of Mummies in the entire world, and they spend most of their time asleep - honestly, I'm still hardpressed to figure out how they can have a society or guilds or anything.<br /> <br /> My big issue with the CofD crossover, however? Exarchs versus God Machine versus Judges, etc. Just how many different god-level supernaturals claim to control the world and its fate? Why aren't they at war with each other, considering they're not working together? There are just too many world spanning powers that control everything to the point it doesn't all fit. I don't think we can have them all working in the same setting, even with the whole &quot;shrouded in mystery&quot; bits. Something has to give.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very valid point, how does GM interact with the Exarchs? Those two are the players with the biggest scope of all god-like antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-28-2016, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:02:03-07:00","id":902018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901973#post901973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My big issue with the CofD crossover, however? Exarchs versus God Machine versus Judges, etc. Just how many different god-level supernaturals claim to control the world and its fate? Why aren't they at war with each other, considering they're not working together?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do we know they're <i>not?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:02:23-07:00","id":902019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901989#post901989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I am harassing people? I made a question, explained why I think so, and waited for answers... At which point did I claim &quot;I am right, all must agree with my point&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't, and didn't. But you could if you wanted, its what a lot of posters do. But I wasn't accusing you of doing it, you just asked a question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-28-2016, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:13:12-07:00","id":902026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901973#post901973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My big issue with the CofD crossover, however? Exarchs versus God Machine versus Judges, etc. Just how many different god-level supernaturals claim to control the world and its fate? Why aren't they at war with each other, considering they're not working together? There are just too many world spanning powers that control everything to the point it doesn't all fit. I don't think we can have them all working in the same setting, even with the whole &quot;shrouded in mystery&quot; bits. Something has to give.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another possibility, rather than fighting or working together, could be that they are all the same thing. Perhaps the exarch are simply the equivalent of infrastructure for the god machine inside the supernal realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:43:50-07:00","id":902041,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the supernatural isn't all that secret in CofD. People don't like to talk about it much, because it's uncomfortable and most folks world prefer to just keep pretending everything is normal and there's no giant squid at the breakfast table. But they know, even if they won't admit it to themselves.<br /> <br /> Rose Bailey has said on these forums that in CofD, pretty much everyone at least has a friend who has had a supernatural experience. I would argue the same is true in real life; the difference is, in CofD, the majority of those experience were actually supernatural. But that doesn't change what most people think about those stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-28-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:52:23-07:00","id":902045,"title":"","content":"All questions that an ST has to answer for their individual games if they choose to have all these globe spanning things in their campaign. <br /> <br /> I deliberately cut my games down to the first seven games (Vampire through Geist), merged the God Machine and Principle and made it operate based entirely on the local Command/Control structure, and removed the global spanning organizations. I like my games local, and I like them being distinct from each other. The first seven games also cover pretty much all the unique archetypes from later games if I need an NPC appearance, so I don't feel the need to throw in a Beast if I want a dragon or gorgon to show up, or Mummy if I want an Egyptian themed undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T09:29:19-07:00","id":902098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901973#post901973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Vampires' Predator Aura ability detect anyone with auras automatically, so that means they can instantly tell werewolves and mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires' predatory aura lets them detect <i>other vampires</i> by sensory input, which is not nearly that broad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I believe that any supernatural can see the Horror super-imposed over the Beast. </div> </div> </div>When they use an Atavism. Passing Resemblance would be useless otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T10:00:58-07:00","id":902118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902041#post902041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the supernatural isn't all that secret in CofD. People don't like to talk about it much, because it's uncomfortable and most folks world prefer to just keep pretending everything is normal <b>and there's no giant squid at the breakfast table.</b> But they know, even if they won't admit it to themselves.<br /> <br /> Rose Bailey has said on these forums that in CofD, pretty much everyone at least has a friend who has had a supernatural experience. I would argue the same is true in real life; the difference is, in CofD, the majority of those experience were actually supernatural. But that doesn't change what most people think about those stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.anaitgames.com/images/uploads/2014/02/octodad-lado.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\">You rang?</span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:55:23-07:00","id":902195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901340#post901340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I think Changelings are more common then Sib Eaters, perhaps closer in sizexto mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is probably true that they are more common than Sin Eaters - That said, it also depends on what kind of changeling you are talking about. They are taken throughout time and space to exist in other worlds, and many of them have been there so long they can no longer return. Its safe to assume that there are a large number of changelings - though whether or not they populate -this- world more than others would depend on how many actually managed to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T13:58:52-07:00","id":902275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902098#post902098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires' predatory aura lets them detect <i>other vampires</i> by sensory input, which is not nearly that broad.</div> </div> </div> </div> Incorrect. Read the side bar in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T14:02:58-07:00","id":902278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902195#post902195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is probably true that they are more common than Sin Eaters - That said, it also depends on what kind of changeling you are talking about. They are taken throughout time and space to exist in other worlds, and many of them have been there so long they can no longer return. Its safe to assume that there are a large number of changelings - though whether or not they populate -this- world more than others would depend on how many actually managed to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div> That sounds more like a 1e Changeling. In 2e you can be turned into any extreme form by the True Fae, but you turn back into a humaniod form when you escape to the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:33:15-07:00","id":902324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902278#post902278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds more like a 1e Changeling. In 2e you can be turned into any extreme form by the True Fae, but you turn back into a humaniod form when you escape to the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Correct. And not every changeling is part of a Freehold. Some even prefer to live inside the Hedge. Many people can be Fetches without knowing, the temporal distortion of Arcadia and the Hedge can send changelings forward and backward in the timeline, they can get trapped in the Hedge/Skein, and more. The point is that their population is hard to pin down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:41:49-07:00","id":902452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902278#post902278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds more like a 1e Changeling. In 2e you can be turned into any extreme form by the True Fae, but you turn back into a humaniod form when you escape to the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't referring to form being the reason they could not escape - assuming that Faerie still has a partially linear temporal connection to the Mortal Realm (that is to say, anyone escaping faerie will return -after- they were taken and not before), and unless they are changing it, former mortals who've been in Arcadia for so long that the world itself has shifted into something unrecognizable have no touchstone that can bring them back to this world - what rare points of memory a woman has who was taken in the year 1880 may not (indeed, in most cases -will not-) be applicable to the year 2016. - These changelings have existed in Arcadia so long that until they die, there is no hope for them - and it may be that they only die whenever their Fae Lords say they die, and not a moment sooner. <br /> <br /> Of course, if Faerie does -not- have a partially linear temporal connection to earth, then things get even more weird and the number is much, much higher and lower at the same time as those in Faerie still exist, do not yet exist, and may never exist as the story goes on. *Disbelieves this for the sake of his sanity*<br /> <br /> My point though is basically what GibberingEloquence said - the numbers of changelings are kind of hard to determine, because there are more than what you see - a lot more. The amount of changelings in earth right now could be a mere triillionth of the amount of changelings that actually exist in Arcadia at this point in Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T20:19:16-07:00","id":902460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902275#post902275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Incorrect. Read the side bar in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. &quot;When Kindred notice werewolves&quot; and &quot;may[,] with Storyteller discretion&quot; do not translate to &quot;Vampires can detect any other kind of supernatural being with an aura 'similar to' their predator aura as a matter of course.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:58:29-07:00","id":902546,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> I'm now just imagining a changeling coming back 2 centuries after they were taken and despite having been gone so long they see people from their old life. One a vampire who has endured the centuries. Another a great beast nearing the end of their life. A ghost or two of people she use to know who have become folk tales. And so on. Despite how everything they know should be gone all too much is familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:20:05-07:00","id":902557,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2909_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2909\" data-vbnamecard=\"2909\">Mr.F.I.X.</a> *Whispers* There are exceptions to every rule. In fact, you may go so far as to say that it's... a Loophole *G*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T03:05:22-07:00","id":902599,"title":"","content":"I've always liked to think that there are only, like, 12 people in the entire world not involved in some sort of supernatural conspiracy. Everyone's just keeping such a tight lid on all the secrets that no-one notices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T03:23:58-07:00","id":902604,"title":"","content":"One of the core assumptions of 2E is that no one has escaped contact with the supernatural in some way - it's one of the five basic breaking point questions included in character generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:00:20-07:00","id":902628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals#post901159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> (This might be rambling a bit, bear with me please)<br /> <br /> <br /> The default Chronicles of Darkness idea is that is &quot;our world but (supernaturally) grim&quot;, and this supernatural is caused by several beings from mythology and such; my peeve is that currently there are too many supernatural beings and societies to be secret! We have: Vampires, Mages, Werewolves, Changelings, Sin-Eaters, Mummies, Beasts, low-power psychic/magicians/skinchangers, ghosts, spirits, etc.<br /> <br /> The secret keeping powers and effects (The lie, mascarade, Lunacy, Mask, etc) can account for people not knowing in an individual basis, the problem is aggregation, CoD is supersaturated with suernatural beings, which since have become so abundant and numerous, are no longer SUPERnatural (definition: <i>departing from what is usual or normal</i> especially so as to appear to transcend the laws of nature)<br /> <br /> In a chronicle that assumes all the gamelines are valid, isn't the world overpopulated with magical beings?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really, there aren't too many supernatural creatures.<br /> We always go from the assumption that people don't know about the supernatural,, but that's a flawed assumption in many cases. Even in the real world, many people believe in those things.<br /> There's been many reports of supernatural creatures appearing in public such as the Popobawa. Those stories are then attributed to collective hysteria and such.<br /> People still murder women and children for being witches to this day, while elsewhere self prolaimed mediums and psychic advertise their talents and for billions more the existence of gods, angels and demons makes no doubt.<br /> For many people, the supernatural is just a fact of life, like the weather. I've personally had people laugh at me for suggesting that they hadn't really been hexed!<br /> <br /> In the Chronicles of Darkness, things are merely more sinister. There too people believe in witches and monsters; the difference is that we are told they're right.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:02:46-07:00","id":902629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902460#post902460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did. &quot;When Kindred notice werewolves&quot; and &quot;may[,] with Storyteller discretion&quot; do not translate to &quot;Vampires can detect any other kind of supernatural being with an aura 'similar to' their predator aura as a matter of course.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> You are taking things vastly out of context. First of all, the bit about werewolves and their aura isn't optional or &quot;with Storyteller discretion.&quot; It flat out says that Kindred detect them. And the developers have stated that the intent of the game is that, when a vampire and werewolf meet up, they instantly recognize each other. There is no room for debate here. Vampires detect werewolves as a matter of course. I'm sorry, but you are mistaken on this account.<br /> <br /> The bit about ST discretion actually says &quot;Other creatures in the World of Darkness may exhibit predatory auras with Storyteller discretion.&quot; Not that the ST decides if a vampire detects someone with an aura, but that the aura exists at all. There is no ST discretion with mages - we know they have an aura. Its in the rules; unless you're making some changes in game, detection is on. I suppose one could argue that its not a &quot;predatory&quot; aura, and therefore doesn't count, but that feels like a stretch to me.<br /> <br /> Now, Changelings and Beasts? These don't necessarily have auras by default. These are the kinds of guys that ST discretion bit apply to, deciding there's an aura for detection. However, as per playtest rules, all you need to see past the Mask are supernatural senses (which vampires have), so an aura is a moot point. As for Beast, even with the superimposed image when using an Atavism, I found that its pretty common for Atavisms to be on all the time. I made no assumptions about which way an ST would rule when it came to these latter two, because its simply unnecessary.<br /> <br /> This is the trend that 2e, as a whole, seems to be moving towards and embracing as a whole. You can houserule things differently, but its pretty clear that vampires can detect more than other vampires by RAW. That ALL supernaturals detect others with fairly high ease.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;notice&quot; bit? You're exaggerating with the difficulty of it. Its the same difficulty vampires have recongizing each other, which, from how the game plays out, is not difficult at all. Unless someone is actively hiding (which is a stretch to assume) or using magic to hide/strengthen Mask, all it takes is a casual brush, an errant sniff, a glance around a room. Given the context of our discussion (if supernaturals will be in the dark about each other), that's all that's necessary to break open the entire secret. And that's all that matters. &quot;Notice&quot; isn't a big restriction for the matter at hand. We're not worried about detecting every last supernatural, we just need a few to break everything open, and the Law of Averages is on the vampire's side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T16:19:58-07:00","id":903079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902629#post902629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You are taking things vastly out of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I. Am I really.<br /> <br /> There is a question-slot devoted to &quot;Is this person a supernatural creature?&quot; with a mage's nimbus given as a specific example in Auspex 2's Uncanny Perception power.<br /> <br /> If that was only supposed to be useful in a scenario where a Clash of Wills would have to be won, <i>don't you think there would have been a note?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, the bit about werewolves and their aura isn't optional or &quot;with Storyteller discretion.&quot; It flat out says that Kindred detect them. And the developers have stated that the intent of the game is that, when a vampire and werewolf meet up, they instantly recognize each other. There is no room for debate here. Vampires detect werewolves as a matter of course. I'm sorry, but you are mistaken on this account. </div> </div> </div>I am mistaken on the account of &quot;werewolves and vampires being similarly predatory aura-having supernatural beings with innate suites of sensory tools that make it straightforward enough to assume they can spot each other for what they are with relatively little difficulty does not inherently translate to vampires having an omnilateral capacity to spot any kind of monster innately&quot;? Do tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bit about ST discretion actually says &quot;Other creatures in the World of Darkness may exhibit predatory auras with Storyteller discretion.&quot; Not that the ST decides if a vampire detects someone with an aura, but that the aura exists at all. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Predatory aura&quot; is a term with a specific case and does not immediately unpack to &quot;every supernatural being's aura effect counts as a predatory aura for the purposes of vampiric detection.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no ST discretion with mages - we know they have an aura. </div> </div> </div>Yup!<br /> <br /> You'll notice <i>even mages can't usually spot it casually.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the &quot;notice&quot; bit? You're exaggerating with the difficulty of it. </div> </div> </div>It's rather difficult for me to exaggerate when the operative word in that quote was &quot;werewolves.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T16:23:50-07:00","id":903084,"title":"","content":"It's also perhaps worth mentioning that werewolves also get harder to detect <i>while in human form </i>as being supernatural, and they get paradoxically, better at it the more &quot;predator&quot; become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T21:10:59-07:00","id":903256,"title":"","content":"The question of how many supernatural residents are too many really comes down to what kind of chronicle you're running. If it's one based around a society with role play interaction, friendly and hostile, than you need enough to have such a society (note they don't all have to be from the same splat, as long as they interact with each other). Also if you intend to use other supernatural characters as antagonists and significant npcs. If on the other hand you are playing a 'lone wolf' style of story, with a solitary supernatural working with normal people and dealing with either mortal or extremely rare supernatural plots you only want a few or none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T04:58:21-07:00","id":903397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903079#post903079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I. Am I really.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, you are.<br /> <br /> Vampires can detect werewolves by aura automatically. This is a given. The write up of Nimbus in Mage says that those with an aura (not a predatory aura, just an aura) are sensitive to those others with auras, and it works both ways. Therefore, vampires can detect mages by their aura. The books are clear that vamps, wolves, and mages can sense each other's auras. This &quot;aura&quot; is called something different in each game - predator's aura, feral mein, and nimbus respectively, and not &quot;predator aura.&quot; And yet, its clear that vampires can sense werewolf's aura despite not being called that outside the vampire side bar.<br /> <br /> The intent of the authors is pretty clear, and that's before we get to the writers flat out saying that the intent is for supernaturals to detect each other automatically. There's no other way of putting this. The rules support vampires sensing others with auras automatically by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a question-slot devoted to &quot;Is this person a supernatural creature?&quot; with a mage's nimbus given as a specific example in Auspex 2's Uncanny Perception power. </div> </div> </div> See, this is what I mean by taking things out of context. The existance of one power does not negate another. This entire line of thinking is a red herring. But, lets indulge it for the sake of argument.<br /> <br /> There are half a million reasons why you could ask this; ST ruled no aura, Clash of Wills, human psychic, more information based on what kind of aura you're sensing, etc. More importantly, it could also be a carryover from 1e's aura sight and not realizing it is potentially redundant. Or a design decision to help people think of this new ability as the replacement of Aura Sight and to highlight why. This, in no way, negates how auras work.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, your entire objection using this is that there should be a side bar saying its only useful for Clash of Wills? Words are a primium. I see no reason to have a detailed explanation for something so minor. Its presence, or lack thereof, has no bearing on this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll notice <i>even mages can't usually spot it casually.</i> </div> </div> </div> You are mistaken. Go read Nimbus section in the Mage core; that's pretty much the opposite of what happens. They notice the predator aura of vampires, and the feral mein of werewolves.<br /> <br /> Secondly, why should it matter if mages can spot something casually or not? <i>We're talking about vampires. What mages can or cannot do has no bearing on this discussion</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm done here; there's really nothing more to say. Vampires can use Predator's Aura and their other innate senses to tell if someone they run into is another supernatural template. This is consistantly true across all 2e gamelines save Demon - werewolves, mages, beasts and changelings all have innate senses that detect other supernaturals as well as their own kind. Its a general trend of 2e as a whole. The default assumption of 2e is that, baring the use of hiding abilities, supernaturals recognize each other on sight.<br /> <br /> This is a direct departure from how 1e handled things, and might take some getting used to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T05:13:29-07:00","id":903404,"title":"","content":"So I guess that the Hishu form ability is... Completely fucking worthless in your reading. That's nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T06:25:15-07:00","id":903433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903404#post903404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess that the Hishu form ability is... Completely fucking worthless in your reading. That's nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hishu form ability doesn't have any relation to this discussion at all.... It doesn't help you hide the fact that you're a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T06:58:29-07:00","id":903448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903433#post903433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hishu form ability doesn't have any relation to this discussion at all.... It doesn't help you hide the fact that you're a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally its purpose, genius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T07:06:42-07:00","id":903456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903448#post903448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's literally its purpose, genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, there is no reason to be rude.<br /> Secondly, it has two abilities in my copy with one increases the werewolf's wolf senses, and the other being sheep's clothing. Sheep's clothing does not have any effect on detecting whether or not the werewolf is a werewolf. The text says &quot;Any efforts to pinpoint the werewolf in a crowd or pursue her through populated areas suffer her Primal Urge as a penalty.&quot; It helps you hide, it doesn't help you hide your supernatural nature.<br /> Thirdly, nowhere in form's description does it even suggest that it is meant to help hide from other supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-30-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:20:09-07:00","id":903544,"title":"","content":"&quot;HISHU<br /> Hishu looks every bit the human being. It\u2019s the homo sa-<br /> piens shape Uratha are born into. While it doesn\u2019t afford any<br /> trait benefits over what a human normally possesses, a Hishu<br /> Uratha is more human than human, and blends into a crowd.<br /> \u2022 Perception: +1 die to Perception rolls using wolf senses.<br /> \u2022 Sheep\u2019s Clothing: Any efforts to pinpoint the werewolf<br /> in a crowd or pursue her through populated areas suffer<br /> her Primal Urge as a penalty&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Hunter's Aspect apparently bypasses it as other werewolves are supposed to know each other, but the way the ability reads, you actually have to activate it for it to activate it rather than it being a passive in the background thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Uratha know each other at a glance. Apex predators smell<br /> their own. When inflicting her hunter\u2019s aspect on a victim every<br /> single sense can identify one Uratha to another, as the man,<br /> the wolf, and the spirit all carry a prominent, forceful aura. The<br /> hunter\u2019s aspect forces her aura on her prey. The Uratha lets loose<br /> her predatory bearing, in order to confront and cow an onlooker.<br /> Her auspice determines just how that bearing manifests itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, reading the text, you get &quot;Apex Predators smell their own&quot; which implies that only werewolves automatically know each other. But the rest of the text for Aspect speaks as if Aspect is a triggered, activated attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also don't see where the detect other supernaturals passively effect is for werewolves. You have to get a Gift for that it seems, which I will note applies to every supernatural that isn't a werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, @MCN, you know, we could just <i>ask </i>the authors what they intend. A good chunk of them are on this board for obvious reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-30-2016, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:00:53-07:00","id":903584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903404#post903404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess that the Hishu form ability is... Completely fucking worthless in your reading. That's nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, not really. But the question of whether a vampire can detect a werewolf via their predatory aura is only relevant in the first place if it works on werewolves in hishu or urhan forms - the other three already provide, shall we say, clues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:21:01-07:00","id":903599,"title":"","content":"You can't pick a werewolf in Hishu out of a crowd. If you've got some sort of monster-dar active the werewolf needs to be standing out in some way, probably by talking to you directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:47:40-07:00","id":903653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903599#post903599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't pick a werewolf in Hishu out of a crowd. If you've got some sort of monster-dar active the werewolf needs to be standing out in some way, probably by talking to you directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing that ability listed anywhere, just Sheep's Clothing. I am in a mixed game with other supers, so it would be good to fall back on. Where is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-30-2016, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:11:23-07:00","id":903665,"title":"","content":"That <i>is </i>Sheeps Clothing. That's what the ability does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:19:19-07:00","id":903735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903397#post903397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The write up of Nimbus in Mage says that those with an aura (not a predatory aura, just an aura) are sensitive to those others with auras, and it works both ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Those who are sensitive&quot; is, again, not the same thing as &quot;those who are sensitive to any kind of aura at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therefore, vampires can detect mages by their aura. The books are clear that vamps, wolves, and mages can sense each other's auras.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> You are mistaken. Go read Nimbus section in the Mage core; that's pretty much the opposite of what happens. They notice the predator aura of vampires, and the feral mein of werewolves. </div> </div> </div>&quot;&quot;[The Nimbus is] wholly invisible except when spellcasting, and even then only to Mage Sight most of the time.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages can pit their own Nimbus against the aura as per the \u201cInteractions with Other Auras\u201d rules, below. While <b>characters without Mage Sight cannot see the aura</b>, the subtle cues still affect them with the Tilt. This is almost always imperceptible, but some particularly clued-in witnesses may note when something\u2019s awry.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, your entire objection using this is that there should be a side bar saying its only useful for Clash of Wills? Words are a primium. I see no reason to have a detailed explanation for something so minor. Its presence, or lack thereof, has no bearing on this discussion. </div> </div> </div>My objection is that a simple added phrase would have been all that was needed to make it clear the question was only relevant in cases where a supernatural-occlusion power would otherwise make this non-obvious, particularly given that Vampire specifically has one of those at the root of its core stealth-oriented Discipline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, why should it matter if mages can spot something casually or not? <i>We're talking about vampires. What mages can or cannot do has no bearing on this discussion</i>. </div> </div> </div>If your reading means mages are less capable of spotting other mages than vampires, it is a blatantly flawed reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The intent of the authors is pretty clear, and that's before we get <b>to the writers flat out saying that the intent is for supernaturals to detect each other automatically. There's no other way of putting this.</b> </div> </div> </div>There is, actually: Put your money where your mouth is and cite your claims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-30-2016, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:23:48-07:00","id":903740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903665#post903665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That <i>is </i>Sheeps Clothing. That's what the ability does.</div> </div> </div> </div>...what?<br /> <br /> Sheep\u2019s Clothing: Any efforts to pinpoint the werewolf<br /> in a crowd or pursue her through populated areas suffer<br /> her Primal Urge as a penalty.<br /> <br /> A penalty that ranges from -1 to -5 is hardly immunity, and it says absolutely nothing about concealing the werewolf's true nature to those sensitive to it. What are you talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:42:11-07:00","id":903755,"title":"","content":"Revealing their true nature sounds like a really good way to pinpoint them, if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:54:14-07:00","id":903762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903755#post903755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revealing their true nature sounds like a really good way to pinpoint them, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ehhh.... say you have a tattoo which marks you as a member of a group. You run into a crowd and blend in. Unless you are noticed specifically in that crowd, that tattoo matters little - at least until you are noticed.<br /> <br /> In this analogy, said tattoo would be an aura; my point being knowing someone is supernatural when you look at them isn't the same as actually finding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:07:45-07:00","id":903770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903762#post903762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this analogy, said tattoo would be an aura; my point being knowing someone is supernatural when you look at them isn't the same as actually finding them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, however, mean that knowing someone is supernatural with even basic scrutiny is not the same thing as being able to identify someone as supernatural at a glance (which, absent some really screwed up population dynamics, makes it markedly easier to pick them out of a crowd), which is kind of Elfive's point re: the interface between Sheep's Clothing and remaining &quot;undercover.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:15:36-07:00","id":903775,"title":"","content":"&lt;shrug&gt; One way of looking at Sheep's Clothing for the purposes of this discussion is that a vampire might sense that there is a werewolf present, but not be able to tell <i>who</i> in the crowd it is. If the crowd is, well, one person, this becomes obvious, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:37:42-07:00","id":903783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903770#post903770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, however, mean that knowing someone is supernatural with even basic scrutiny is not the same thing as being able to identify someone as supernatural at a glance (which, absent some really screwed up population dynamics, makes it markedly easier to pick them out of a crowd), which is kind of Elfive's point re: the interface between Sheep's Clothing and remaining &quot;undercover.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm.<br /> <br /> <i>You are on the hunt in the city, walking in their midst looking for food. As you breath in, you smell something amidst the blood - a sound in the hundreds of heartbeats surrounding you. It's not like theirs - it's scent, its sound. It's notably different - not Kindred, for sure, but a predator - a hunter. You look around from person to person, but find no trace of them. You feel a chill down your spine, like they are close - after all, if you noticed them it stands to reason they may have noticed you. You are beginning to feel that the hunter has become the hunted.</i><br /> <br /> My thought is, and this is just my thoughts here - knowing someone is supernaturalat a cursory glance, sniff, sound, etc. is not the same as picking them out of a crowd. It -is- picking them out of a lineup, but that's a wholly different circumstance. A wolf in sheep's clothing by itself is more evident than a wolf in sheeps clothing that blends with the herd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:07:47-07:00","id":903797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903740#post903740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...what?<br /> <br /> Sheep\u2019s Clothing: Any efforts to pinpoint the werewolf<br /> in a crowd or pursue her through populated areas suffer<br /> her Primal Urge as a penalty.<br /> <br /> A penalty that ranges from -1 to -5 is hardly immunity, and it says absolutely nothing about concealing the werewolf's true nature to those sensitive to it. What are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to carify primal urge goes to ten. Standard bonus or penalties have an exception to the max of +/-5 of supernatural effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:35:27-07:00","id":903983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903755#post903755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revealing their true nature sounds like a really good way to pinpoint them, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you're talking like they're immune to such attempts. They aren't. They get to impose a (mild to extreme) penalty on any relevant rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:46:36-07:00","id":903990,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters sound a bit iffy to me in terms of how equipped they are to uphold their own masquerade, even if they are not very populous. Their damage reduction via Plasm alone is visually obvious. Ghostly phenomena in general do not have their version of Lunacy, Quiescence or a Mask. And I don't think Krewes hire trained clean-up teams as a matter of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T03:17:52-07:00","id":904065,"title":"","content":"Yes, but on the other hand, there's less to hide for Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> 42% of people in the USA believe in ghosts, in the United Kingdom a poll found that 52% believe in ghosts. So that's about 134 million people in the USA who believe in ghosts.<br /> <br /> So let's face it, it can't be that much of a secret.<br /> <br /> And if someone found out you can talk to ghosts, they aren't going to bring out the pitchforks shouting &quot;Burn the witch!&quot;<br /> <br /> They might offer $50 to find out where dear Aunt Alice hid the good jewels.<br /> <br /> They might offer the sin-eater their own talk show.<br /> <br /> They might ask to join the sin-eater's new religion.<br /> <br /> They might ask for help in solving crimes.<br /> <br /> They might ask the sin-eater to clean out a haunted house. <br /> <br /> You know, the sort of things that happen with people in real life who claim to be able to communicate with the dead. <br /> <br /> Combine that with the rule that the sin-eaters, as far as I'm aware, have no cultural imperative to keep a masquerade, nothing stops a sin-eater from putting an ad in the yellow pages under &quot;medium.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T05:45:01-07:00","id":904104,"title":"","content":"They might keep the whole &quot;possessed by a powerful ghost-thing&quot; on the down low, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:17:42-07:00","id":904131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=904104#post904104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might keep the whole &quot;possessed by a powerful ghost-thing&quot; on the down low, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trade secrets, man. Can't lose the competitive edge.<br /> <br /> Though, consider the number of people who claim to channel or be possessed by spirits/ghosts/aliens/saints/angels/etc. Again, what do they really have to hide?<br /> <br /> If anything, Sin-Eaters have the <i>best</i> Masquerade - even other supernaturals might not take their existence seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:51:23-07:00","id":904148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=904131#post904131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, consider the number of people who claim to channel or be possessed by spirits/ghosts/aliens/saints/angels/etc. Again, what do they really have to hide?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the crowd was initially excited to hear that John Edwards could speak to a guests' dead mother, they grew anxious when he explained how he could eat her spirit to power his other abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything, Sin-Eaters have the <i>best</i> Masquerade - even other supernaturals might not take their existence seriously. </div> </div> </div>I imagine the only problem with sin-eaters breaking the Masquerade is it would encourage flatscans to meddle. How long until someone finds a gate to the Underworld and decides to drive construction vehicles down there to get building material or more real estate or to use it to dispose of toxic waste or some other wacky idea. Or non-sin-eaters to start collecting ghost anchors and forcing them to do the bidding of their new owner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:03:07-07:00","id":904158,"title":"","content":"Also the dying and coming part might make people get a few ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:28:04-07:00","id":904175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=904158#post904158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the dying and coming part might make people get a few ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shhhh! Sin-Eaters <i>really</i> don't want that one scientifically tested/explored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:03:22-07:00","id":904338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=903990#post903990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sin-Eaters sound a bit iffy to me in terms of how equipped they are to uphold their own masquerade, even if they are not very populous. Their damage reduction via Plasm alone is visually obvious. Ghostly phenomena in general do not have their version of Lunacy, Quiescence or a Mask. And I don't think Krewes hire trained clean-up teams as a matter of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who needs damage reduction when you can respawn!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:22:11-07:00","id":904538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=901343#post901343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I think world governments also help cover stuff up, not just the supernatural communities themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I link you to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.groundzeromedia.org/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.groundzeromedia.org/api/og\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.groundzeromedia.org/\" target=\"_blank\"> GroundZeroMedia.org &mdash; Domain Available </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.groundzeromedia.org/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.groundzeromedia.org/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> GroundZeroMedia.org is available for acquisition. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You are welcome. This is a real person with a real show that sounds like it'd be a parody in a garish satire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:14:43-07:00","id":904798,"title":"","content":"About the aura detection debate.<br /> Vampire Second edition pg 92 top &quot;... Without a Discipline or other ability to mask or suppress the predatory aura, Kindred perceive other vampires as their own kind....&quot; This is about vampires so i would think that even if they find another supernatural being they won't know what it is (unless they had prior contact and knowledge). Now about sheep's clothing, it falls in the &quot;other ability&quot; category and when viewed with an aura detection ability (auspex, mage sight, werewolf gift) they suffer a penalty. For mages its the occultation merit. Both requires that the mage or werewolf doesn't do something like casting a spell or gift or changing form. Its about the passive ability to detect other based on smell, touch or general feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/125-baltazor","name":"Baltazor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:53:34-07:00","id":906381,"title":"","content":"I haven't read most of this thread. Might go back and read it later. The OP's problem might be that of the one where we can only conceive a certain number of individuals as actually being people, because for most of human history this was the average population size of a &quot;tribe&quot;. It's somewhere between 100-200 people. When you're populating most long running chronicles. you want to think of the supernatural splats group being at least that big (or whatever) so you've got some maneuvering room, probably bigger so that &quot;you don't know everyone&quot;. That's all fine (depending on your city size), your problem is now in your head everyone you know is a &quot;Vampire&quot; (splat) or otherwise supernatural. So the whole world must be? because it's really hard to comprehend there are 100,000+ people in this city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:26:26-07:00","id":906667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=902041#post902041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the supernatural isn't all that secret in CofD. People don't like to talk about it much, because it's uncomfortable and most folks world prefer to just keep pretending everything is normal and there's no giant squid at the breakfast table. But they know, even if they won't admit it to themselves.<br /> <br /> Rose Bailey has said on these forums that in CofD, pretty much everyone at least has a friend who has had a supernatural experience. I would argue the same is true in real life; the difference is, in CofD, the majority of those experience were actually supernatural. But that doesn't change what most people think about those stories.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, the mortal population behaves like in &quot;Welcome To Night Vale&quot; but writ large?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:37:35-07:00","id":906674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=906667#post906667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, the mortal population behaves like in &quot;Welcome To Night Vale&quot; but writ large?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Love that comparison <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also where i would see a problem isnt in how the various splat share the world and more how there ennemies (especially those at the ''godlike' level) coexist together. I mean what does the god-machine think of the abyss for example??? So many thing that have unquantifiable power with a vested interest in the world (which is why i usually choose what exist and what doesnt).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:39:54-07:00","id":906675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/901159-too-many-supernaturals?p=906667#post906667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, the mortal population behaves like in &quot;Welcome To Night Vale&quot; but writ large?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. The weirdness isn't usually so obvious, either. Less alien invasions and zombie apocalypses and more group of hikers saw something big and hairy that talked to them of secret worlds, or a single person encounter that's even easier to dismiss. Someone goes into their basement and a glowing tree is growing out of the floor, they think it's a dream but it promises to grant their wishes if it just does some things for it and keeps it secret. Everyone knows about the old lady down the street with the house full of cats, but only one person noticed how strangely intelligent the cats seemed, and he's sure they killed his dog because they know he noticed, but he can't tell anyone or he'd seem crazy. You caught your boss with that intern, at first you thought they were making out but when he let go of her she fell to the floor, limp and bloodless. He said something, you forgot what, but now you've got a promotion with a massive raise, less hours to work, and feel stronger than ever, you wouldn't even think of betraying him. You just stumbled on that drug deal, you really had nothing to do with it, but they chased you for miles until you fell in that pit that wasn't a pit. The ants bit and stung you for what seemed like an eternity, and something's changed in you, and you find yourself able to control them.<br /> <br /> There's so many reasons not to bring it out to the public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}